# VideoBrief — AI pipeline

## Abstraction

```text
AIProvider
  classifyVideo
  generateSections
```

Implement with Vercel AI SDK. Default model: `analysisConfig.model.defaultId` (OpenRouter). Do not call a vendor SDK from UI or Server Actions.

## Pipeline stages (domain)

1. Workspace stub exists; fetch metadata + English transcript (YouTube `categoryId` as optional hint)
2. `classifyVideo` → `{ isEducational, confidence, topic? }` — **no** section skeleton, **no** LLM questions
3. If educational and topic known → optional familiarity select (3 levels)
4. If appropriate → optional length select (3 levels; default from profile `summary_style` or moderate)
5. Persist per-video prefs on the analysis row (empty answers allowed)
6. `generateSections` → `{ title, startTime, endTime, body }[]` using transcript subset + profile + prefs
7. If not educational → skip familiarity; still generate sectioned summary using profile when present; soft disclaimer in UI

Ambiguous classification → **prefer educational**.

## Validation (required)

```text
LLM → structured output → Zod.parse → app types → DB
```

Never persist raw/unvalidated model JSON.

## Personalization

Change emphasis, depth, and framing — not invent unrelated content. Non-edu still may use profile for framing.

## Cost

Classify stays tiny. Generate is one transcript-shaped call after prefs. Cap `maxOutputTokens` on generate. Do not regenerate classify in order to write bodies.
